# igt-lenovo-gem.list: the IGT buffer and submission subtests of the Lenovo's
# conformance cases (tests/native/gpu.cases), which lenovo.sh runs part by
# part through igt.sh, on Rach2's i915 and on Debian's Linux alike; Linux's
# results are its run of this list in the conformance step's Debian boot.
#
# A line is `igt@TEST`, every subtest of the test program TEST, or
# `igt@TEST@PATTERN`, its subtests that the shell pattern PATTERN matches in
# the IGT stage's subtest-list.txt. A part begins with `# part NAME`. The
# list leaves out, as Linux's display run did, every subtest that hangs the
# GPU on purpose, which 78-6c's hang cases take, and those that suspend the
# machine, swap, fork many clients or pin CPUs, which test other parts of
# the kernel. In each part the tests that keep the GPU busy with IGT's
# spinners come last.
# part gem-1
